{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/184826-flowers-of-hell-show-of-power-p-114","id":184826,"title":"Flowers of Hell: Show of Power, p. 114","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-30T08:21:57-07:00","id":184826,"title":"Flowers of Hell: Show of Power, p. 114","content":"Just curious, but why should this power fail if a member of the copied supernatural type can see it's not genuine? Inflict a Condition or cause a penalized Compromise roll, sure, but fail outright?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T09:40:43-07:00","id":184911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/184826-flowers-of-hell-show-of-power-p-114#post184826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just curious, but why should this power fail if a member of the copied supernatural type can see it's not genuine? Inflict a Condition or cause a penalized Compromise roll, sure, but fail outright?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026It <i>doesn't.</i><br /> <br /> <i>If the power fails,</i> then an appropriate supernatural observer <i>can tell that something's up</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T14:57:28-07:00","id":185082,"title":"","content":"But it states that the activation roll is contested &quot;vs. highest Wits + Supernatural Tolerance of observers of emulated supernatural type&quot;, with a Failure resulting in no effect, and with a Dramatic Failure &quot;Not only does the demon fail to imitate the power, she loses the ability to use her Embeds, Exploits, and demon form abilities until the end of the scene.&quot; The contesting dice pool involved implies that the very act of observation by relevant parties can cause the failure of the power to activate, which is what doesn't make sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T15:06:34-07:00","id":185128,"title":"","content":"You're talking about a half-improvised trick of a supernatural group whose primary mode of disguise relies on people thinking of their cover identity as something expected trying to duplicate the supernatural powers of a <i>different</i> supernatural group through channels that only manifest themselves to observers if the power activates successfully and asking why onlookers familiar with those channels looking for them and reducing the amount of wiggle room the demon has is a thing that makes sense when macro-scale quantum effects are highlighted at multiple points both in this specific book and throughout the rest of the line so far.<br /> <br /> Think about that for a moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T18:23:30-07:00","id":185282,"title":"","content":"OK, perhaps I didn't word my initial query correctly. The Exploit's description says that a failed roll reveals to any relevant supernatural witnesses the trickery behind the power. However, according to the power's mechanics, the presence of relevant supernatural witnesses causes the power to fail, causing there to be nothing for the witness to see. The reasoning, narrative and otherwise, just seems flawed to me.<br /> <br /> But enough of that. Any suggestions on how to patch it up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T19:11:31-07:00","id":185297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/184826-flowers-of-hell-show-of-power-p-114?p=185282#post185282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But enough of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, this really needs exploring.<br /> <br /> It's an Exploit, which means you're rolling a three-component dicepool against the highest two-component dicepool of <i>relevant supernatural observers</i>. Regardless of the number of successes you get, you emulate the power as though it had been activated with one success by a [Primum] Supernatural Tolerance entity, so all you really need to do is beat a dicepool that for most supernatural entities which it is remotely wise to try to fool in such a manner is going to be around six or seven as a high average. That's not difficult to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> OK, perhaps I didn't word my initial query correctly. The Exploit's description says that a failed roll reveals to any relevant supernatural witnesses the trickery behind the power. However, according to the power's mechanics, the presence of relevant supernatural witnesses causes the power to fail, causing there to be nothing for the witness to see. The reasoning, narrative and otherwise, just seems flawed to me. </div> </div> </div>&quot;If you fail this roll, the roll's failure lets any members of the supernatural type who are watching you determine that you just tried to fake whatever power you tried to replicate&quot; is not much of a &quot;the presence of relevant supernatural witnesses causes the power to fail&quot; scenario, for all that it looks like a minor one. Lots of supernatural entities add their Supernatural Tolerance to rolls to detect supernatural phenomena relevant to them.<br /> <br /> What's the takeaway here?<br /> <br /> 1) Don't try to fool powerful supernatural beings if you don't want to get caught.<br /> 2) Don't try to fool supernatural beings into thinking you're one of them by trying to replicate powers that can't be set up away from observation.<br /> 3) Tricking supernaturals into thinking you're a different kind of supernatural, like a ghost or a spirit or something mysterious that they haven't encountered, as suggested by Deep Cover, is a fantastic use of this power.<br /> and, because tetragrammatical convention demands it,<br /> 4) Just using this power as a catalog of useful effects you can Megaman into your supernatural repertoire absent the involvement of other supernatural beings is <i>also</i> a fantastic use of this power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T08:04:01-07:00","id":185517,"title":"","content":"OK, fair enough. Your points, taken with the Core Book's discussion on 'optional resistances', answer most of my concerns.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And now, a tangent: As an Exploit, Show of Power can mimic most any ability the demon has personally witnessed/experienced. With such a large pool of potential effects, how far should it be limited if used in an Exploited Gadget? A single effect would be in line with other Exploits, but debatably, so could limiting the gadget to effects of a single supernatural type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","user":"shkspr1048","date":".  New Thought 07-01-2014, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T03:41:29-07:00","id":186161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/184826-flowers-of-hell-show-of-power-p-114?p=185297#post185297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the takeaway here?<br /> <br /> 1) Don't try to fool powerful supernatural beings if you don't want to get caught.<br /> 2) Don't try to fool supernatural beings into thinking you're one of them by trying to replicate powers that can't be set up away from observation.<br /> 3) Tricking supernaturals into thinking you're a different kind of supernatural, like a ghost or a spirit or something mysterious that they haven't encountered, as suggested by Deep Cover, is a fantastic use of this power.<br /> and, because tetragrammatical convention demands it,<br /> 4) Just using this power as a catalog of useful effects you can Megaman into your supernatural repertoire absent the involvement of other supernatural beings is <i>also</i> a fantastic use of this power.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm going to add to your assessment here. I suspect that this power's raison d'etre is to actually mimic said supernatural in their own society. What do I mean?<br /> <br /> You can make pacts with other supernaturals. You can take their place in said supernatural society. This power lets you hide out with others in said society without people raising a question: &quot;Wait, what do you mean you can't cast Mage Sight?&quot; or &quot;What do you mean, you can't cross into the shadow via locus?&quot;<br /> <br /> The whole resistance thing makes it so that you have to keep a low profile when under cover as a supernatural, yeah. Its risky, for obvious reasons. But the whole point is that you're supposed to try and fool other supernaturals that you are One Of Them.<br /> <br /> You have to be sneaky about it, sure. Slip away to cast the mage sight, maybe. Be the last one to cross over. You're in a spy genre, so you have to act like a spy to duplicate these effects. Be underhanded, be distracting, don't draw attention to yourself. Stay under the radar. That's why the resistance roll - to push you into situations where you can't just show off with it. Its enough power to make it seem like you're One of Them, but not enough to do much useful otherwise.<br /> <br /> Remember that your ST has complete control over what supernaturals you meet, and what powers you get to actively observe. They're not going to be offering you a swiss army knife of various powers to bust out whenever you get away from the chosen supernatural - all supernaturals are, after all, in secret societies themselves, who hide their powers from non-members as well. Its unrealistic to call it a mega-man power, because being a megaman doesn't rely on becoming his targets and sneaking into said society. Also, remember that using powers your Cover shouldn't have access to is probably Acting Out of Cover, and will likely prompt Compromise checks independent of the usual Exploit check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-02-2014, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T03:54:53-07:00","id":186183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/184826-flowers-of-hell-show-of-power-p-114?p=185517#post185517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: And now, a tangent: As an Exploit, Show of Power can mimic most any ability the demon has personally witnessed/experienced. With such a large pool of potential effects, how far should it be limited if used in an Exploited Gadget? A single effect would be in line with other Exploits, but debatably, so could limiting the gadget to effects of a single supernatural type.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think you're approaching this backwards. Design what you want the gadget to do first, and what makes sense for the thing your installing into. A knife won't be granting you Mage Sight, for instance, even if it was letting you mimic a different Death spell. A pair of contact lenses or glasses could likely mimic mage sight stuff, but not control ghosts.<br /> <br /> I would also say that it can't &quot;grow&quot; with new observations of non-demon magic. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}